@startuml intentional-backfill
title US-10: Intentional Backfill - Consumer Rewound to Rebuild State

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Developer
participant "Correlation\nWorker" as Worker
queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as Kafka
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j
database "Kafka\noffset store\n(__consumer_offsets)" as Offsets

note over Neo4j
  Neo4j restarted.
  Entity relationship graph lost.
  Must be rebuilt from event history.
end note

Developer -> Worker : stop correlation worker
Developer -> Offsets : reset consumer group offset\nto timestamp T (start of retention window)

note over Offsets
  Offset reset is explicit and intentional.
  Kafka retains all events within
  the configured retention window.
end note

Developer -> Worker : restart correlation worker

Worker -> Kafka : consume from reset offset T
Kafka --> Worker : all position events from T onwards

loop for each replayed event
  Worker -> Neo4j : MERGE proximity edges\n(idempotent - no duplicates created)
end

note over Worker
  Graph rebuilt from event history
  without re-querying OpenSky or AIS.
  Same mechanism works for corrected
  anomaly rules - rewind and re-evaluate.
end note

Worker -> Worker : offset caught up\nprocessing live events

@enduml
